From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] comctl32, user32: Windows 7's edit borders, drop-down lists, status bar, tabs, progress and track bars

Purpose: draw the common controls of programs in the Windows 7 shell
session as Windows 7's comctl32 6 does.
Windows behavior (measured on Windows 7 SP1 with screenshots of the
same test window and tests/status-height.c):
- a drop-down list (CBS_DROPDOWNLIST) is drawn with the style's
  CP_READONLY part over the whole box, hot under the mouse anywhere,
  and its arrow alone (CP_DROPDOWNBUTTONRIGHT, normal state) in a 17
  pixel column at the right edge, inset a pixel at the top and bottom;
  the text and the focus rectangle sit three pixels in, up to three
  pixels before the arrow; no highlight when focused;
- a status bar is as tall as its default font plus the borders and its
  vertical border on both sides (24 pixels), whatever font WM_SETFONT
  gave; its text starts two pixels into a part;
- a group box's frame is a pixel lower and its caption a pixel further
  right, check box and radio button labels a pixel further left (as XP
  measured before); list box text starts two pixels into the item;
- an edit control's border is the style's edit border for its scroll
  bars (EP_EDITBORDER_*), hot under the mouse and focused;
- DrawFocusRect inverts a checkerboard aligned to the DC, its pixel
  (0, 0) left alone;
- a tab's text starts at the padding from the item's edge when the tab
  is wider than it (minimum width, selected tab) instead of being
  centered, and an unselected tab's text is a pixel lower; unselected
  tabs are as tall as the item, the last of a row two pixels narrower;
  a tab control takes the focus when clicked only with
  TCS_FOCUSONBUTTONDOWN (tests/tab-focus.c);
- a progress bar is smooth, drawn with the style's translucent bar
  (PP_TRANSPARENTBAR, no content margins) and its fill over it, from
  the client area's edge;
- a track bar's thumb is 19 pixels long (22 with ticks on both sides,
  24 with a selection range as well; seven less than a shorter client,
  six with ticks on both sides), a one-sided thumb as wide as its 11x19
  part scaled to that, the channel half a thumb plus three pixels from
  the edges and the ticks a pixel nearer the thumb
  (tests/trackbar-size.c gives Windows 7's values exactly).
Wine before: an XP-style drop-down list, a status bar 4 pixels taller,
centered tab labels, text a pixel off, a focus rectangle dotted from
its corner, tab controls focused by any click, a progress fill inset
a pixel, and XP's 21 pixel track bar thumb.
Change: as above, for the Windows 7 shell session (WIN4WINE_SHELL=win7;
the drop-down list for a version 4 style with CP_READONLY; the tab
focus for the opted-in external shell).
Evidence: those parts of the test window are pixel-identical to
Windows 7's apart from ClearType's colors, also hot and focused.
Scope: Windows 7 shell session, and the tab focus for every external
shell.
